---
import { localeFromPath } from '@portfolio/i18n';
import { isrMonthly2026 } from '@portfolio/calculators';
import { Table, TableHeader, TableBody, TableRow, TableHead, TableCell } from '@portfolio/ui/components/table';
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import IsrCalculator from '../../components/calculators/IsrCalculator';
const locale = localeFromPath(Astro.url.pathname);
const amount = (value: number) => new Intl.NumberFormat(locale === 'es' ? 'es-MX' : 'en-US', { minimumFractionDigits: 2 }).format(value);
---
<ToolLayout title="ISR salary calculator" description="Calculate the ISR withheld from your monthly salary in Mexico with the 2026 tariff and the employment subsidy." category="Taxes" image="isr" checked="Rates checked November 11, 2026" app>
  <IsrCalculator locale={locale} client:load />
  <div slot="guide" class="flex flex-col gap-8">
    <div class="prose-copy"><h2>How much ISR comes out of your pay?</h2><p>Enter your gross monthly salary. The calculator finds your row in the monthly tariff of Article 96 of the ISR law, applies its rate to the amount above the lower limit, adds the fixed fee, and then subtracts the employment subsidy if your income qualifies.</p></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>Which tariff does it use?</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>The 2026 monthly tariff from Annex 8 of the Miscellaneous Tax Resolution (DOF, December 28, 2025). Amounts are in MXN.</p></div>
        <div class="mt-4 mb-6 rounded-xl border"><Table className="text-xs tabular-nums"><TableHeader><TableRow><TableHead>Lower limit</TableHead><TableHead>Fixed fee</TableHead><TableHead>Rate on the excess</TableHead></TableRow></TableHeader><TableBody>{isrMonthly2026.map(([lower, fixed, rate]) => <TableRow><TableCell>{amount(lower)}</TableCell><TableCell>{amount(fixed)}</TableCell><TableCell>{rate}%</TableCell></TableRow>)}</TableBody></Table></div></details>
      <details><summary>How does the employment subsidy work?</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>The 2026 decree (DOF, December 31, 2025) grants 15.02% of the monthly UMA, MXN 535.65, to employees whose monthly income does not exceed MXN 11,492.66. In January it was MXN 536.21. It only reduces the tax: if it is larger than the ISR, the withholding is zero and the difference is not paid to you. Both values are editable.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What is not included?</summary><div class="prose-copy"><p>Employee social security (IMSS) contributions, Infonavit credit payments, and other payroll deductions are not part of this estimate. Exempt income, such as part of the Christmas bonus or savings fund, should be left out of the amount. Workers who earn only the minimum wage are not subject to withholding; this calculator does not apply that exemption. Your employer may calculate per pay period, and the annual return can change the final tax. This is an estimate, not tax advice.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolLayout>
